WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.266 --> 00:00:01.434 align:start size:94% position:6%
-The last time you were here
was a while back,

00:00:01.434 --> 00:00:05.472 align:start size:94% position:6%
but I had -- you sent over
a mascot to the show.

00:00:05.472 --> 00:00:05.905 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Yep.

00:00:05.905 --> 00:00:08.241 align:start size:94% position:6%
-This is the mascot you made
for a field piece.

00:00:08.241 --> 00:00:08.942 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
That's Chiijohn.

00:00:08.942 --> 00:00:09.876 align:start size:94% position:6%
-That's right.
That's right.

00:00:09.876 --> 00:00:14.414 align:start size:94% position:6%
I remember, I texted you
not long before they arrived

00:00:14.414 --> 00:00:16.316 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
-Kind of just really like

00:00:16.316 --> 00:00:19.619 size:88% position:44%
selling you on the idea
as a small unit of time.

00:00:19.619 --> 00:00:21.421 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yes.
-It's like "This will take 10,

00:00:21.421 --> 00:00:22.422 size:75% position:38% line:92%
15 minutes maximum."

00:00:22.422 --> 00:00:25.658 align:start size:94% position:6%
What I did not realize,
at that point,

00:00:25.658 --> 00:00:27.160 align:start size:94% position:6%
was that they don't speak
at all.

00:00:27.160 --> 00:00:32.298 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yes.
-So, there are Japanese
mascots -- mascotees?

00:00:32.298 --> 00:00:32.932 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:00:32.932 --> 00:00:36.636
I don't know what the technica
job title is -- inside there

00:00:36.636 --> 00:00:38.038 align:start size:94% position:6%
So, they don't
speak English,

00:00:38.038 --> 00:00:40.940 align:start size:94% position:6%
but they also
won't speak at all.

00:00:40.940 --> 00:00:41.408 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Right.

00:00:41.408 --> 00:00:43.443
-So, they had a translator
so I could speak to them.

00:00:43.443 --> 00:00:46.112
But then, they would not respond
out of character at all.

00:00:46.112 --> 00:00:48.815 align:start size:94% position:6%
They basically went
full Daniel Day-Lewis

00:00:48.815 --> 00:00:51.184 align:start size:94% position:6%
inside two otter costumes.
Yeah.

00:00:51.184 --> 00:00:55.255
-And it is -- I will tell yo
first of all, it was true.

00:00:55.255 --> 00:00:56.456 align:start size:94% position:6%
You said, "This will take
10 minutes."

00:00:56.456 --> 00:00:57.991 align:start size:94% position:6%
It absolutely did.
-You're welcome.

00:00:57.991 --> 00:01:00.193 align:start size:94% position:6%
-It is so unnerving...
-Yes.

00:01:00.193 --> 00:01:02.262 align:start size:94% position:6%
-...to have a silent masco
stare at you.

00:01:02.262 --> 00:01:06.466 align:start size:94% position:6%
-It is really -- It seems
charming, and initially it is.

00:01:06.466 --> 00:01:09.436 align:start size:94% position:6%
But then, you look through
the grill of the eyes,

00:01:09.436 --> 00:01:12.138 align:start size:94% position:6%
and you see the silhouette
outline of someone

00:01:12.138 --> 00:01:15.508 align:start size:94% position:6%
you don't know
who will not speak to you.

00:01:15.508 --> 00:01:16.976 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
-And whenever you give them,

00:01:16.976 --> 00:01:18.411
like, basic instructions,
they'll just respond --

00:01:18.411 --> 00:01:20.747 align:start size:94% position:6%
again, in character --
with a kind of "hee, hee, hee.

00:01:20.747 --> 00:01:22.015 size:88% position:44% line:92%
And you go "Okay. Okay."

00:01:22.015 --> 00:01:23.583 align:start size:94% position:6%
I get the "hee, hee, hee.
I really do.

00:01:23.583 --> 00:01:25.585 align:start size:94% position:6%
But can we go over there
for a second take?"

00:01:25.585 --> 00:01:28.288 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
-It is genuinely unnerving

00:01:28.288 --> 00:01:29.756 align:start size:94% position:6%
But --
they didn't speak a single -

00:01:29.756 --> 00:01:30.990 align:start size:94% position:6%
I was with them
for two days.

00:01:30.990 --> 00:01:32.292 align:start size:94% position:6%
They didn't say
a single word.

00:01:32.292 --> 00:01:35.228 align:start size:94% position:6%
And then, during breaks,
they were still in character

00:01:35.228 --> 00:01:36.696 align:start size:94% position:6%
kind of grabbing
each other's tail

00:01:36.696 --> 00:01:41.134 align:start size:94% position:6%
while everyone else is eating,
going, "Is this all day?"

00:01:41.134 --> 00:01:43.736
-It's also unnerving to thin
that you spent that much tim

00:01:43.736 --> 00:01:47.140 align:start size:94% position:6%
with two people you could no
describe to the police.

00:01:47.140 --> 00:01:48.108 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:01:48.108 --> 00:01:51.010 align:start size:94% position:6%
If they did something terrible
they would be like,

00:01:51.010 --> 00:01:52.946
"What did they sound like?
What did they look like?"

00:01:52.946 --> 00:01:53.680 size:84% position:42% line:92%
And you'd have nothing.

00:01:53.680 --> 00:01:54.914 align:start size:94% position:6%
-That's right.
You say "I don't know."

00:01:54.914 --> 00:01:56.616 size:78% position:39%
They say, "This story
just doesn't add up.

00:01:56.616 --> 00:01:57.717 align:start size:94% position:6%
Two days,
they said nothing."

00:01:57.717 --> 00:02:02.622 align:start size:94% position:6%
"No. I can describe the outlin
of a human head."

00:02:02.622 --> 00:02:05.859 align:start size:94% position:6%
-It was like sort of,
"Oh, and they did this a lot."

00:02:05.859 --> 00:02:07.060 align:start size:94% position:6%
-They go "hee, hee, hee"
a lot --

00:02:07.060 --> 00:02:08.895 align:start size:94% position:6%
presumably,
after they kill.

00:02:08.895 --> 00:02:10.330 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-[ Laughs ]

00:02:10.330 --> 00:02:13.800 align:start size:94% position:6%
We are talking right now
on Super Tuesday.

00:02:13.800 --> 00:02:14.334 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Yeah.

00:02:14.334 --> 00:02:15.368 align:start size:94% position:6%
-When this is over,
will you go home?

00:02:15.368 --> 00:02:16.836 align:start size:94% position:6%
Will you watch the returns
of Super Tuesday?

00:02:16.836 --> 00:02:20.507
-No. I mean, it's -- look,
I'm glad it's finally here

00:02:20.507 --> 00:02:21.674 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
-But there is a lot --

00:02:21.674 --> 00:02:23.610 align:start size:94% position:6%
there has been a lot of talk
about it today.

00:02:23.610 --> 00:02:24.978 align:start size:94% position:6%
It's kind of been irritating
watching the news today,

00:02:24.978 --> 00:02:27.714 size:78% position:39%
just having them say,
"Who do you think is
gonna win this state?

00:02:27.714 --> 00:02:29.582 align:start size:94% position:6%
Who do you think is
gonna win this state?

00:02:29.582 --> 00:02:31.084 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
Just wait.

00:02:31.084 --> 00:02:33.286 align:start size:94% position:6%
You're about
to find out.

00:02:33.286 --> 00:02:35.221 align:start size:94% position:6%
People on the --
they're like kids...

00:02:35.221 --> 00:02:36.856 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
--...in the back row of a car.

00:02:36.856 --> 00:02:41.027 align:start size:94% position:6%
"Oh, who -- who -- who's gonna
win Alabama, dad?"

00:02:41.027 --> 00:02:44.230 line:92%
"Wait for the exit polls.

00:02:44.230 --> 00:02:45.732 align:start size:94% position:6%
Wait for the polls
to close.

00:02:45.732 --> 00:02:48.801 align:start size:94% position:6%
Don't make me turn
this democracy around."

00:02:48.801 --> 00:02:51.738
They just --
They just cannot help themselves

00:02:51.738 --> 00:02:53.373 align:start size:94% position:6%
but want to know.
-Yeah.

